flow "Sliding window rate limiter"
summary "Weights the previous and current window counts to enforce rate limits smoothly and prevent fixed-window boundary bursts."
tags rate-limiting resilience api
level intermediate
source "https://blog.cloudflare.com/counting-things-a-lot-of-different-things/"
related distributed-systems/rate-limiter-token-bucket

node client "Client" actor
node limiter "Rate Limiter" service tone=primary
node store "Window Counters" db
node api "Backend API" service
edge client > limiter
edge limiter > store
edge limiter > api
array win "Window state (limit=4/min)" keys=prev,curr,est = 2 1 2.5

scenario sliding "Weighted sliding window allows normal traffic"
  step arrive "Request arrives at 01:15 (25% into window)"
    "At `01:15`, the current minute is 25% elapsed, so the rolling 60s window overlaps **75%** of the previous minute (`00:00-01:00`)."
    send client > limiter "GET /api"
    state limiter active
    send limiter > store "read prev=2, curr=1"
  step check "Compute weighted count"
    "Instead of storing every request timestamp, the sliding-window counter estimates `prev * 0.75 + curr = 2*0.75 + 1 = 2.5`. That is under the limit of `4`."
    pulse store
    callout limiter "2 * 0.75 + 1 = 2.5 < 4 -> allow"
  step allow "Increment current counter and forward"
    "The limiter increments `curr` to `2` (`est = 3.5`) and forwards the request to the backend."
    send limiter > store "INCR curr -> 2"
    label win#curr "2"
    label win#est "3.5" with
    send limiter > api "GET /api"
    state limiter,api success

scenario boundary-burst "Boundary burst blocked across minute edge" from=sliding/arrive
  step spike-end "Client sends 4 requests at 00:59"
    "A client fires the full limit of 4 requests right before the minute rolls over (`00:59`). A **fixed window** would reset to `0` at `01:00` and allow 4 more — doubling the real rate."
    label win#prev "4"
    label win#curr "0" with
    label win#est "4.0" with
    state win#prev warning with
    callout store "00:59: previous window full (4)"
  step spike-start "More requests arrive at 01:01"
    "Just 2 seconds later (`01:01`), another burst arrives. The sliding window still weights **98%** of the previous minute: `4 * 0.98 + 0 = 3.92`, so adding this request reaches `4.92 > 4`."
    send client > limiter "burst at 01:01"
    send limiter > store "read prev=4, curr=0"
    label win#est "4.92 (>4)"
    state win#est error with
  step reject "Reject with 429 to stop double-rate burst"
    "Because the weighted estimate exceeds `4`, the limiter returns `429 Too Many Requests`. The rolling overlap eliminates the fixed-window boundary loophole."
    state limiter error
    effect limiter shake
    send limiter > client "429 Too Many Requests"
    callout api "No 2x burst reaches backend"
